fixup(git): close discard traversal bypass + add WSS e2e

Addresses two remaining Copilot review threads on PR #115:

1. `is_safe_rel` traversal bypass: a pathspec like `a/../tracked.txt`
   passed the lexical containment check (because the target resolves to
   a path inside the worktree), but the classification step matches the
   index against the un-normalized string — so it missed the exact-file
   probe, fell through to the untracked-deletion branch, and the OS
   resolved `..` at unlink time and would have removed the tracked file.
   Refuse ANY `..` component up-front (component-scan on the input) so
   the bypass cannot reach classification. New unit test
   `discard_refuses_traversal_bypass_into_worktree` seeds `tracked.txt`,
   attempts `discard(["a/../tracked.txt"])`, and asserts the request is
   refused as `-32602` AND the tracked file is still intact.

2. WSS end-to-end coverage: per `packages/intentd/AGENTS.md`, every new
   `git.*` router method needs a WSS e2e driving the real `/ws`
   transport. Add `crates/intentd/tests/e2e_wss_git_discard.rs` with two
   scenarios — happy path (restore-tracked + delete-untracked in one
   call, asserting the `{ ok, paths }` envelope shape from PROTOCOL.md
   §5) and refusal path (`a/../tracked.txt` ⇒ `-32602` envelope shape
   from §9, tracked file untouched).
